    "text": "Step 2: Notice that for \\( n = 2, 3, 4, \\dots, 7 \\), we have \\( p(n) = \\frac{n}{n^2 - 1} \\). Substituting these values into the definition of \\( q(x) \\):\n- For \\( n = 2 \\), \\( q(2) = (2^2 - 1)p(2) - 2 = 3 \\cdot \\frac{2}{3} - 2 = 0 \\).\n- For \\( n = 3 \\), \\( q(3) = (3^2 - 1)p(3) - 3 = 8 \\cdot \\frac{3}{8} - 3 = 0 \\).\n- For \\( n = 4 \\), \\( q(4) = (4^2 - 1)p(4) - 4 = 15 \\cdot \\frac{4}{15} - 4 = 0 \\).\n- For \\( n = 5 \\), \\( q(5) = (5^2 - 1)p(5) - 5 = 24 \\cdot \\frac{5}{24} - 5 = 0 \\).\n- For \\( n = 6 \\), \\( q(6) = (6^2 - 1)p(6) - 6 = 35 \\cdot \\frac{6}{35} - 6 = 0 \\).\n- For \\( n = 7 \\), \\( q(7) = (7^2 - 1)p(7) - 7 = 48 \\cdot \\frac{7}{48} - 7 = 0 \\)."
